  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ensuring Equitable Access of Refugees with Temporary Protection to Quality Health Services in the Republic of Moldova</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed joint programme between IOM, UNFPA, UNICEF and WHO was developed to ensure refugees with temporary protection have equitable access to quality health services in the Republic of Moldova. The programme was closely coordinated with key stakeholders, namely the Ministry of Health and the National Health Insurance Company and based on critical gaps identified. The expected results are twofold, namely that refugees with temporary protection use quality health services, including compensated medicines and medical products; and the Government of the Republic of Moldova finances and monitoring the health service provision for refugees in evidence-based, sustainable, and unified manner.</narrative>
  </description>
